  "question": "Background / Context\nThe project involves enhancing a user management system named UserFrosting, built on a PHP-based web framework. UserFrosting distinguishes itself by providing a fully-functional user management application that can be easily extended to meet custom requirements using a modular system known as \"Sprinkles.\" This system addresses the modern development needs by offering a comprehensive set of tools for building scalable applications.\n\n Objectives\nThe primary objective of the project is to provide robust user management features, including user authentication, role-based access control (RBAC), and administrative capabilities for managing users. It aims to deliver a maintainable and extendable framework that follows modern development practices.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n- Administrators: Manage user accounts, permissions, and roles.\n- Developers: Extend and customize the application using Sprinkles.\n- End Users: Register, log in, and interact with the application.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n1. User Authentication: \n   - Users can sign in and maintain persistent sessions with a \"remember me\" feature.\n   \n2. Admin User Management:\n   - Administrators can view, search, sort, create, and edit user accounts, including resetting passwords.\n   - Tools are available to enable or disable users and manage user permissions.\n   \n3. Roles and Permissions:\n   - Utilize powerful RBAC to define access rules and manage permissions through a role management interface.\n   \n4. Extensibility:\n   - Implement custom features using modular Sprinkles without altering the core codebase.\n   - Support for themes, plugins, and more.\n   \n5. User Dashboards:\n   - AdminLTE-themed dashboards for providing users with an interactive interface.\n\n6. Activity Tracking:\n   - Log user activities with details such as IP address and activity type.\n   \n7. Password Management:\n   - Support for password resets and verifications with expiration and completion tracking.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n1. Performance:\n   - Optimization through asset bundling with Node.js and caching for templates and routes.\n   \n2. Documentation:\n   - Comprehensive guides explaining the usage, features, and rationale behind the system components.\n   \n3. Maintainability:\n   - Separation of concerns to minimize code complexity and facilitate future upgrades.\n\n4. Scalability:\n   - Designed to accommodate growth and incorporation of additional user roles and permissions without impacting performance.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0073\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_name` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `active` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  `verified` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `registered_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `last_login_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `remember_token` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `users_user_name_unique` (`user_name`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `users_email_unique` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `roles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `roles_name_unique` (`name`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `roles_slug_unique` (`slug`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `permissions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `permissions_name_unique` (`name`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `permissions_slug_unique` (`slug`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_roles` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`,`role_id`),\n  KEY `user_roles_ibfk_2` (`role_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_roles_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_roles_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `role_permissions` (\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`role_id`,`permission_id`),\n  KEY `role_permissions_ibfk_2` (`permission_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `role_permissions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `role_permissions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`permission_id`) REFERENCES `permissions` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `activities` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `ip_address` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `activity_type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `activities_ibfk_1` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `activities_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `password_resets` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `expires_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `completed_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `password_resets_token_unique` (`token`),\n  KEY `password_resets_ibfk_1` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `password_resets_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sprinkles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `version` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `enabled` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `sprinkles_name_unique` (`name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
